cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these models, data or code, please cite them as below."
title: "opencif-cfd: the COMSOL models and Python CFD of the CIF dissertation"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-09"
authors:
  - family-names: "Routt"
    given-names: "A. H."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7286-2924"
abstract: >-
  Every computational-fluid-dynamics file behind A. H. Routt's dissertation on Controlled Incremental Filtration
  (CIF) design: the COMSOL Multiphysics models, reports and exports of a single-gap quarter cell (Runs A, B and C) and
  of a five-gap outlet slab at Dinh et al.'s V1 and V3 outlet widths; Python CFD, an independent finite-element Stokes
  solver built on scikit-fem and PyAMG, with its runs; and the comparison of the two codes with ASME V&V 20-2009
  numerical-uncertainty estimates.
keywords:
  - microfluidics
  - controlled incremental filtration
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - Stokes flow
  - COMSOL Multiphysics
  - finite element method
  - verification and validation
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Austin-Routt/opencif-cfd"
